<p>Few places in Texas know floodwater like San Marcos. The city sits where the Hill Country drops off the Balcones Escarpment, and heavy rain on the steep, thin-soiled terrain to the west can send the Blanco River, the San Marcos River, and local creeks up with very little warning. This guide covers flood damage insurance claims in San Marcos: the floods that shaped the area, how flood coverage differs from ordinary water damage coverage, how National Flood Insurance Program (NFIP) policies work, what changed with the 2025 flood maps, and how to protect your claim.</p>

<h2>Flash Flood Alley: San Marcos flood history</h2>

<p>NOAA's Storm Events Database lists 127 flash flood reports and 12 flood reports for Hays County. Flooding can happen in any season, but reports cluster in late spring and fall: June (28 combined flash flood and flood reports), May (24), and October (21) lead the list. Several of those events caused major damage and led to federal disaster declarations.</p>

